#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * Dutch for the lesson CONTENT of the Bee Flow Foundations course (BFSF-474) —
 * the course the Learning Center opens with ("Getting started" and its seven
 * follow-up lessons), plus the intro tour that IS the first lesson, plus the
 * verified-action checklists of those lessons.
 *
 * The Learning Center's chrome already had Dutch (add-nl-learning-center-
 * translations), which is exactly why the bug stung: a Dutch learner got Dutch
 * buttons around English course text. The content itself was never seeded —
 * and until BFSF-474 the quiz choices, sim pairs and launch labels did not
 * even HAVE keys, so the Languages panel could not have held a translation.
 * Those keys are generated now (learn.<lesson>.<step>.choice|pair|item|…),
 * and this migration fills the foundations set.
 *
 * The register follows the English: plain, one idea per sentence, product
 * names ("New Chat", "Privacy Shield", "How I got this answer") kept as the
 * UI spells them. Where the English quotes a Dutch UI string already
 * ("Maak een banner…"), the quote stays as it is.
 *
 * Idempotent: only fills keys that are missing, so a workspace that curated its
 * own wording keeps it. ADD, NEVER RENAME — a renamed key is a screen that
 * silently falls back to English. Auto-runs from server boot
 * (boot/bootMigrations.js). Manual usage:
 *   node server/migrations/add-nl-learning-foundations-translations.js
 */

